# Never ship secrets or local state into an image.
#
# These patterns are deliberately "**/" prefixed. A bare ".env" in a
# .dockerignore matches only the build-context root, so "cv-model/.env" —
# the one holding the API key and the mail password — would have been copied
# straight into the image by the COPY of cv-model/.
.env
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/firebase-key.json
**/*serviceaccount*.json
**/*-firebase-adminsdk-*.json

# Kept on purpose: .env.example documents the settings, and .env.production
# carries the Firebase web config, which is public by design and has to be
# present when the frontend is built.
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.production

# Local environments and caches — rebuilt inside the image.
**/.venv
**/venv
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache

# Local run data. Uploaded CVs, past rankings and the user database — which
# holds password hashes — stay on your machine.
cv-model/storage
cv-model/results.json
honda-hr-frontend/dist
cv-model/web

# Editor and OS noise
.git
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
